# Doctest coverage waivers — shrink-only ratchet.
#
# Names on this file are known-missing public subjects granted a
# temporary waiver from the coverage requirement. `oxitest` treats
# each as a Notice (visible tech debt) rather than an Error under
# `strict = "abort"`. Waivers are shrink-only: removing an entry fails
# if the subject is still missing coverage; adding an entry fails if
# the subject is already covered.
#
# Wayfinder map: #1602. Realizes decision #1604.
#
# NOTE: Public subjects that alias into `oxitest._bridge.*` submodules
# (e.g. `oxitest.mark`, `oxitest.TestResult`) produce
# `doctest.coverage.analysis` errors — the scanner cannot verify their
# docstrings via the alias chain. Analysis errors bypass the waivers
# ratchet entirely (they are not in the "missing subjects" set), so
# listing them here would make them permanently stale. They are left
# out; the analysis errors are visible under `--warnings` but do not
# block the ratchet. Fix by adding docstrings to the aliased sources.
